From 6710e556e2fd1e97c747c796a080fa302c9041ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PathOps <noreply@pathops.dev>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 18:06:03 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] workload: generic workload token exchange

PathOps Decision 0065: one generic RFC 8693 workload token exchange
replaces the service-specific registry and Artifact Store token profiles.
Dex no longer derives an Application from Kubernetes names or labels and
no longer reads the Kubernetes API.

A configured confidential client (the PathOps Tenant Control Plane)
exchanges:

  subject_token  a workload token (ID token type), verified by the
                 configured subject connector: issuer, signature, expiry
                 and audience (patch 0001's subjectTokenAudiences)
  actor_token    an EdDSA JWT of a trusted actor (issuer, audience, kid,
                 lifetime at most 5 minutes) whose subject_token_hash is
                 base64url(SHA-256(subject_token)) and whose
                 target_audience is the requested audience
  audience       a configured output

for a JWT signed with the output's own Ed25519 key, with the output's
issuer and audience, the subject's identity as sub, at most the output's
maxLifetime (less when the actor's token_lifetime asks for less), and the
claims the output lists copied unchanged from the actor's authorization
object. Each output is its own signing authority: two outputs
never share a signing key or an issuer, so a service that verifies only
the signature (not aud or iss) cannot accept another output's token. Dex does not interpret those claims; the actor already decided
them. A token exchange with an actor_token is answered only by this grant
(unsupported when it is not configured). Toward the subject connector it is a token
exchange: a connector limited to grantTypes [token-exchange] serves it.

Configuration (opt-in; without it nothing changes):

  workloadTokenExchange:
    clients: [pathops-tenant-control-plane]
    subjectConnector: k8s-cell
    actors:
      - issuer: pathops-tenant-control-plane
        audience: pathops-workload-exchange
        keys: [{kid: tcp-workload-1, ed25519: <base64url public key>}]
    outputs:
      - audience: pathops-registry
        issuer: https://dex.example.org/registry
        signingKeyFile: /etc/dex/registry/registry.key
        keyID: registry-1
        maxLifetime: 30m
        claims: [access, pathops_application]
